We compare, holding weights, data, optimiser and steps fixed:
• dense: all-to-all mixing (n2 links per layer);
• local: k = 1 at every layer;
• fixed: one hypercube dimension, the same at every layer (the control for “sparse but not
rotated”);
• rot: hypercube dimension ℓmod b at layer ℓ;
• mixa: local and long-range layers alternate, the long jumps visiting each scale once (32, 16, 8, 4, 2, 1
for n = 64);
• hybrid: the mixa backbone with two of the layers replaced by standard multi-head attention.
The exact layer lists are given as short schedule strings in Appendix A.

